{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No current FDA/DailyMed label identified.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2012/005856s021ltr.pdf"],"proposed_value":"Potential fetal malformations and serious side effects; reserve Tridione for petit mal seizures not controlled by less toxic drugs.","rationale":"The FDA accessdata label for Tridione (trimethadione) exists and contains a top-of-label warning. DailyMed was not used for this check.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"trimethadione","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"trimethadione","rationale":"FDA label identifies TRIDIONE as trimethadione.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tridione","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Tridione","rationale":"FDA label and NCBI MeSH support Tridione as an alias/brand for trimethadione.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"Troxidone; Trimetin","rationale":"NCBI MeSH lists Troxidone and Trimetin as entry terms for trimethadione. Tridione is already captured as the trade name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"Tridione","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Tridione; Troxidone; Trimetin","rationale":"PubMed/MeSH search should include the MeSH entry terms to avoid duplicate alias rows and improve retrieval.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"No - discontinued FDA Orange Book product","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"No - discontinued/not marketed in U.S.","rationale":"The no-availability conclusion is supported. Epilepsy Foundation notes Tridione tablets were no longer made/distributed, and FDA Orange Book change data show discontinued tablet listing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.epilepsy.com/stories/community-corner-new-drug-alerts","https://www.fda.gov/media/130048/download"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy (specific FDA-labeled seizure category not available from Orange Book listing)","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Petit mal/absence seizures refractory to treatment with other drugs (historical FDA-labeled indication).","rationale":"FDA label states Tridione is indicated for control of refractory petit mal seizures; the current row incorrectly says no specific FDA-labeled seizure category is available.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A 0%: no current FDA/DailyMed label identified; FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide adverse-event percentages.","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA-approved Tridione label lists adverse reactions but does not provide incidence percentages.","rationale":"FDA label lists adverse reactions by category, but without percentage incidence; the no-label rationale is contradicted by the FDA label.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide metabolism information.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver - trimethadione is demethylated by liver microsomes to active metabolite dimethadione.","rationale":"FDA label provides metabolism information identifying liver microsomal demethylation.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic/liver microsomal","rationale":"The label identifies liver microsomal metabolism, so the filter should not remain limited/unknown if hepatic is an available category.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not describe enzyme induction or inhibition.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA label does not state that trimethadione induces or inhibits drug-metabolizing enzymes.","rationale":"N/A is plausible, but the row rationale should cite the FDA label rather than saying no label exists.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide half-life.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA label does not state a half-life.","rationale":"FDA label describes absorption, metabolism, and excretion but does not state a half-life.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not describe QT effect.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA label does not describe a QT interval effect.","rationale":"No QT text was found in the FDA label, but the no-label rationale is incorrect.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide a maximum approved daily dose.","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"2.4 g/day (usual adult dosage range 0.9-2.4 g/day).","rationale":"FDA label provides adult dosage range and divided dosing.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide a minimum effective dose.","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Adult initial dose 0.9 g/day; FDA label does not state a fixed minimum effective dose and says maintenance should be the least amount required to maintain control.","rationale":"FDA label provides initial adult dosing and maintenance principle.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide dosing.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"3 or 4 divided doses daily.","rationale":"FDA label states adult and pediatric dosing is given in 3 or 4 divided doses.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located; FDA Orange Book confirms historical U.S. product approval/listing but does not provide mechanism of action.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Unclear/limited - FDA label identifies trimethadione as an oxazolidinedione antiepileptic and describes animal anticonvulsant activity, but does not state a molecular mechanism.","rationale":"FDA label provides limited pharmacology; Orange Book alone is not the best mechanism source.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata Tridione label (Description/Clinical Pharmacology)","rationale":"The mechanism/pharmacology facts are supported by the FDA label, not the Orange Book products file.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Limited","rationale":"The FDA label gives limited pharmacology but not a molecular mechanism.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Historical oral capsule; historical oral solution; historical oral tablet (not marketed in U.S.)","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Historical oral capsule; historical oral solution; historical oral tablet (not marketed in U.S.)","rationale":"Historical tablet formulation is directly supported by FDA label/Orange Book change data; capsule and solution are consistent with FDA-derived historical product data, but the row should retain Orange Book as the named source for those forms.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.fda.gov/media/130048/download"]},{"current_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","rationale":"FDA Orange Book data documentation uses this phrase for products approved before Jan 1, 1982; FDA change data also show the Tridione tablet as a legacy product.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.fda.gov/media/130048/download"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA accessdata/Drugs@FDA Tridione (trimethadione) label; NCBI MeSH/PubMed search audit; Epilepsy Foundation availability note.","rationale":"DailyMed should not be used for the black-box field, and the FDA accessdata label is needed for indication, dosing, metabolism, adverse reactions, and warning facts.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293","https://www.epilepsy.com/stories/community-corner-new-drug-alerts"]}],"generic_name":"trimethadione","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT for trimethadione was identified; no RR50 value should be calculated.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=%28trimethadione+OR+Tridione+OR+Troxidone+OR+Trimetin%29+%28placebo+OR+randomized+OR+double-blind%29+epilepsy","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","