not available from Orange Book listing)","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Petit mal/absence seizures refractory to treatment with other drugs (historical FDA-labeled indication).","reason":"FDA label gives the seizure category.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy","field":"filter_epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Petit mal/absence seizures","reason":"Align filter with FDA-labeled indication.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No current FDA/DailyMed label identified.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"Potential fetal malformations and serious side effects; reserve Tridione for petit mal seizures not controlled by less toxic drugs.","reason":"FDA accessdata label contains a top warning; DailyMed was not used.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2012/005856s021ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed search on 05-20-2026: no current label found for terms [trimethadione; Tridione].","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata Tridione (trimethadione) label, NDA 005856/S-021, approved 06-06-2012; top warning/boxed warning verified 05-21-2026.","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA sources only; FDA label was identified.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2012/005856s021ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"fda_black_box_warning_verified","proposed_value":"05-21-2026","reason":"FDA warning re-verified during this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_